From a5beab590c42200e2aea1dee060c412fc37da9a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: astrangedaytoday15-dev <342675337+astrangedaytoday15-dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 03:48:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] World 3D R2 + R3: continent stream round the followed
 unit, models and NPCs

Needs mod-wowmin-telemetry with the continent radius stream
("wowmin stream <map> 0 <player> <yards>"); without it World 3D keeps
markers and says the models are unavailable.

- R2: TelemetryStream.watch takes a follow (player, radius) for instance 0
  and renews with the radius form; one stream per continent, the latest
  watcher wins. /api/stream accepts instance=0 with unit and radius,
  checked by parseStreamFollow (letters-only name, 10-250 yd) as they go
  into a console command. streamPositions passes them on.
- R3: World 3D opens that stream for the followed unit (reopened on a new
  unit, map or radius) into its own stores, and poses players and
  creatures with Instance Watch's builder (getInstanceUnitPoses now takes
  its stores; Instance Watch's are the default), with strikes, spell
  effects and game objects. NPC nameplates from creature info; markers
  only for units without a model yet. Radius picker 30 / 50 / 100 (a
  player's view distance) / 250, default 30, remembered.
- Closer zoom (16 yd across); the framed height shrinks with the zoom.
- Tests: follow parsing and the subscribe commands.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
